WEBVTT

NOTE Narration by an AI voice: Matilda (XrExE9yKIg1WjnnlVkGX), eleven_v4.

intro
00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:09.140
Copilot measures a slow SPL2 search, then asks Splunk AI Assistant to optimize it.

separate-counts
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:15.860
The baseline counts attempts, then counts failures in a second branch.

wildcard
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:22.120
It starts with wildcard index selection, then filters for this sourcetype.

two-branches
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.160
Both branches read the same data independently.

join
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.920
A join matches the aggregates by service and version.

extra-work
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:37.200
That adds work to produce just four summary rows.

skill
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:43.540
The performance skill compares job metrics with query structure.

evidence
00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:49.500
Completed-job status gives us a measured baseline.

baseline
00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:57.180
About ninety-two seconds, 1.42 million events, four rows.

single-aggregation
00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:05.140
Splunk AI Assistant counts attempts and failures together in one aggregation.

direct-index
00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:11.980
It scopes the search to demo_soc instead of every index.

same-report
00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:18.420
Service, version, attempts, failures, and rates remain.

verify-next
00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:23.120
The final run checks both runtime and output rows.

same-event-count
00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.280
Both jobs report the same 1.42 million events and four rows.

matching-rows
00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:35.420
All four service and version rows match in value.

runtime
00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:41.360
Runtime drops from ninety-two seconds to two and a half.

speedup
00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:47.620
About thirty-seven times faster, with the same four rows.

why-fast
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:53.080
One aggregation removes the second branch and join.

close
00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:58.600
Same failure-rate report, delivered in seconds.
